{
  /*
    tetragrammatonPermutation: the Twelve Banners of the Name, Crowley,
    777 (London and Felling-on-Tyne: Walter Scott Publishing Co., 1909),
    col. CXL. No scan of the 1909 printing was found at a stable address
    (archive.org has only later typed texts), so none is linked. Each is
    one of the twelve orders of the Name's letters, each once, and the
    schema's description says how the two He's, h and H, are told apart.
    Until magick-data 0.2.1 Cancer had Leo's hvyH and Sagittarius
    Capricorn's Hyhv.

    hebrewLetterId: the simple letter the Golden Dawn gives the sign, as
    the table of attributions by Hebrew letter in Regardie, The Golden
    Dawn, vol. 4 (Chicago, 1940), p.298 (archive.org
    IsraelRegardie-TheGoldenDawn-Vol4-1940, leaf n290) has it, with the
    trump of the path the letter is on.
  */
